proof: aaru5 | fedora | node-floppy
date: 2026-07-15
lane/VM: test-fedora (Fedora 44 KDE), repo COPR gmipf/media-preservation
user groups: "gmipf wheel" (NO cdrom/disk/plugdev) -> groupless
device: NEC USB UF000x floppy (USB-UFI 0409:0040) -> /dev/sda (media present)
mechanism: packaged udev rule /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-aaru5-floppy.rules
  (ENV{ID_TYPE}=="floppy", TAG+="uaccess"); NO cap needed.

Method: fresh USB enumeration per state (sticky uaccess db tag), poll ACL ~2s.
Floppy is not ID_CDROM; systemd grants nothing (70-uaccess.rules has no floppy clause).

--- RED (no floppy rule, fresh enumeration) ---
  CURRENT_TAGS=:systemd: ; ACL ABSENT ; dd -> Permission denied

--- GREEN (ONLY 70-aaru5-floppy.rules present, fresh enumeration) ---
  node=/dev/sda ; ACL present @~2s (user:gmipf:rw-) ; tag=uaccess ; dd=OK

VERDICT: PROVEN. aaru5's packaged 70-aaru5-floppy.rules alone grants the floppy node
uaccess to a groupless user on a fresh plug; without any floppy rule it is denied.
